Prerequisites

1. Install mise
   curl https://mise.run | sh
2. Toolchain + deps
   mise install
   uv sync

Environment

1. Create env file
   cp .env.example .env
2. Set at least:
   GEONODE_USER=<value>
   GEONODE_PASS=<value>
   GEONODE_GATEWAY=fr|fr_whitelist|us|sg
   GEONODE_TYPE=residential|datacenter|mix
   GEONODE_COUNTRY=<country_code_or_empty>
   GEONODE_LIFETIME=3..1440 (minutes)

Run

Default behavior:
- Jobs and results are stored in `out.state.sqlite3`.
- `out.csv` and `out.errors.csv` are exported atomically from the state database.
- If `out.state.sqlite3` already has successful RUCs, they are skipped automatically.
- If the state database does not exist yet, existing `out.csv` success rows are imported once as completed jobs.
- Sticky sessions are always used (one concurrent sticky session per worker).
- OSIPTEL's current endpoint is queried over HTTP through the sticky proxy.
- `--page-size 5000` usually fetches all lines for a RUC in one request; pagination remains as a fallback for larger result sets.

uv run robot \
  --input samples.csv \
  --output out.csv \
  --workers 3 \
  --page-size 5000 \
  --session-budget 4 \
  --wait-min-s 6 \
  --wait-max-s 10 \
  --ban-cooldown-s 180 \
  --env-file .env
